{
  "slug": "guide/components/outputs",
  "title": "Custom events with outputs",
  "description": "A component can emit custom events by declaring outputs.",
  "source": "https://angular.dev/guide/components/outputs",
  "status": "reviewed",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "tip",
      "text": "This guide assumes you've already read the [Essentials Guide](essentials). Read that first if you're new to Angular."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A component can emit custom events by declaring **outputs**:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "file": "custom-slider.component.ts",
      "lang": "ts",
      "code": [
        "import {Component, output} from '@angular/core';",
        "",
        "@Component(/* ... */)",
        "export class CustomSlider {",
        "  // Declare an output named 'valueChanged'.",
        "  valueChanged = output<number>();",
        "}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "You can listen for these events in parent component templates using event binding:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "file": "app.component.html",
      "lang": "html",
      "code": [
        "<custom-slider (valueChanged)=\"onValueChanged($event)\" />"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "id": "emitting-events",
      "text": "Emitting events"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The `output` function returns an `OutputEmitterRef`. You emit an event by calling its `emit` function:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "file": "custom-slider.component.ts",
      "lang": "ts",
      "code": [
        "export class CustomSlider {",
        "  valueChanged = output<number>();",
        "",
        "  updateValue(newValue: number) {",
        "    this.valueChanged.emit(newValue);",
        "  }",
        "}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "id": "output-aliases",
      "text": "Output aliases"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Similar to inputs, you can specify an `alias` for an output to change the property name used in templates:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "file": "custom-slider.component.ts",
      "lang": "ts",
      "code": [
        "export class CustomSlider {",
        "  valueChanged = output<number>({alias: 'valueChange'});",
        "}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "id": "declaring-outputs-with-decorator",
      "text": "Declaring outputs with the @Output decorator"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Angular also supports declaring outputs using the `@Output` decorator and `EventEmitter`:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "file": "custom-slider.component.ts",
      "lang": "ts",
      "code": [
        "import {Component, Output, EventEmitter} from '@angular/core';",
        "",
        "@Component(/* ... */)",
        "export class CustomSlider {",
        "  @Output() valueChanged = new EventEmitter<number>();",
        "}"
      ]
    }
  ]
}